  "Introduction": "Wait on Me is the fourth extended play by South Korean singer Kai, released on April 21, 2025, by SM Entertainment.[2] The EP contains seven tracks including two singles, \"Adult Swim\" and \"Wait on Me\".\n\nBackground and release\nAccording to SM Entertainment's third quarter earnings report in November 2024, Kai would be releasing a new EP in the first quarter of 2025.[3]\n\nOn March 5, 2025, Star News reported that Kai was preparing for his comeback in music scene in April 2025, with music video scheduled to film next week.[4] On March 31, SM Entertainment confirmed the release date of Kai's fourth EP to be on April 21.[5] In addition, the EP has a total of seven tracks including the title track of the same name and the first single \"Adult Swim\" to be released 19 days prior. The pre-orders also began at various online and offline music stores.[6] On April 1, the website 'Behind Wait' (kai-waitonme.com) was created in conjunction with Kai's fourth EP and the schedule of various contents of the EP.[7] The next day, Kai confirmed to hold his first showcase since debuting as a soloist in 2020 at Yes24 Live Hall in Gwangjin District, Seoul from 20:00 (KST) and would also be live stream online through Exo's YouTube and Weverse channels.[8]\n\nThe pre-release single \"Adult Swim\" was released along with its music video on April 3.[9][10] A music video for the b-side song \"Walls Don't Talk\" was released on April 15th.[11]\n\nThe title track \"Wait On Me\" was released on April 21 alongside the full album.[12]",
